<!--
  SecretPrinter.Respond6.csproj

  Written by Claude (Anthropic model, Claude Opus 5) at the direction of
  Edwin West, for the SecretPrinter project. Reviewed by a human before merge.

  An experiment, not a component of the service. It answers one question: will
  iOS accept an A record delivered over IPv6 mDNS transport and then open an IPP
  connection over IPv4 to port 631? The result is recorded in
  docs/findings/2026-09-06-ipv6-mdns-transport.md.

  Deliberately carries no [Requirement] markers, for the same reason as
  SecretPrinter.Respond: the requirements in README.md describe the service, and
  this tool will be superseded by it. Marking a throwaway experiment as
  implementing service requirements would make the coverage matrix say something
  untrue.

  A correction. An earlier version of this comment claimed the project was kept
  out of SecretPrinter.slnx so that it would not participate in SpecCheck's
  requirement coverage. That was false. SpecCheck scans compiled
  SecretPrinter*.dll files found beneath the directories it is told to search,
  and reads requirement markers from the assemblies; one carrying no markers
  contributes nothing and cannot cause a failure. Solution membership never
  affected the coverage matrix, and this project's output was already being
  scanned whenever it had been built. It is now in the solution, so CI compiles
  it and it cannot rot unnoticed.

  Delete this project once IPv6 transport is part of SecretPrinter.Mdns.

  Common build settings, including the target framework, come from
  Directory.Build.props at the repository root and are not restated here.

  Note for future editors: MSBuild project files are XML, and an XML comment
  cannot contain a double hyphen. Command line examples containing option
  flags therefore belong in README.md, not in a comment here.
-->
<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <OutputType>Exe</OutputType>
    <RootNamespace>SecretPrinter.Respond6</RootNamespace>
    <AssemblyName>SecretPrinter.Respond6</AssemblyName>
    <!-- Experiment only: never packed, never signed, never released. -->
    <IsPackable>false</IsPackable>
  </PropertyGroup>

</Project>
